<%# Live response tally, replaced over Action Cable as answers land.

    `live` is false on the page's own first render and true on every broadcast,
    which is what distinguishes "here are the numbers" from "these just changed" —
    the second gets the pulse and the refresh affordance, because the charts below
    are still showing the older aggregation until the creator asks for a rebuild.
    Rebuilding them automatically would re-aggregate every response for every
    viewer on every submission, and move the page under someone reading it.

    The headline is the one number people open this page for, so it keeps its
    34px; the supporting counts are .ask-stat tiles — the same component Ask
    Verto's scope folder uses — because they were three interchangeable grey
    phrases in a row that wrapped mid-phrase at 1440. %>
<div id="results-live" class="rh-tally">
  <div class="rh-count">
    <span class="rh-count-num<%= " is-pulsing" if live %>"><%= responders %></span>
    <span class="rh-count-word">response<%= responders == 1 ? "" : "s" %></span>
  </div>

  <div class="ask-stat rh-stat" style="--stat-accent:#01EACB;">
    <span class="ask-stat-dot"></span>
    <span class="ask-stat-num"><%= completed %></span>
    <span class="ask-stat-label">completed</span>
  </div>

  <%# Did anyone join? Only shown once the creator has switched the ask on —
      on every other Verto it would be a permanent zero that means nothing.
      A count, deliberately, and never a list: the creator is being told how
      many people want to hear what happened, not who they are. %>
  <% if survey.join_prompt? %>
    <div class="ask-stat rh-stat" style="--stat-accent:#8B85FF;"
         title="People who asked to hear what came of this Verto">
      <span class="ask-stat-dot"></span>
      <span class="ask-stat-num"><%= survey.player_claims.count %></span>
      <span class="ask-stat-label">asked to hear</span>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <% if live %>
    <%# Reloads just the results frame, so the breakdown rebuilds on demand
        rather than on every incoming answer. %>
    <%= link_to "↻ Refresh breakdown",
          survey_results_path(survey, segment: params[:segment]),
          data: { turbo_frame: "results-feed" },
          class: "rh-refresh" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
